        "title": "Early Naturalists - Aristotle, Linnaeus, Buffon, John Ray",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Natural history is the systematic observation, description, and classification of\nliving things and their environments. Before the 18th century, it was encyclopedic\nbut unsystematic. The figures here imposed order on the chaos of biological diversity."
    },
